{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.lepton_continuant_binet","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.lepton_continuant_binet","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.linFunctionalK_exactly_geometric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.linFunctionalK_exactly_geometric","kind":"theorem","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/lepton_continuant_binet.lean#L235-L248","doc":"**The fine-tuned direction does not escape either.**\n\nOne might hope to cancel the growing `qⁿ` component and get a different\nlaw from the survivor.  The readout `α = β q⁻¹` kills `B`, and the\nrecursion then becomes *exactly* geometric with ratio `q²` — no\nremainder at all, hence still log-linear.  So the one direction in the\nfamily that could have behaved differently is the most rigid of all:\nthere is no member with a bent tower. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.linFunctionalK_two_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.linFunctionalK_two_step","kind":"theorem","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/lepton_continuant_binet.lean#L197-L233","doc":"**Two-step rigidity of every `H₂(q)`-linear readout.**\n\n```\n  φ(n+2) = q² · φ(n) + (−1)ⁿ (q − q⁻¹) B q⁻ⁿ,      B = α − β q⁻¹.\n```\n\nEvery linear readout of the lepton braid advances by the *same* factor\n`q²` per generation step, corrected only by a term decaying like `q⁻ⁿ`.\nThe readout choice `(α, β)` survives solely inside `B`, i.e. it can\nrescale the vanishing correction but not the `q²`.\n\nThis is the invariant that prunes the search (AGENTS.md formalize-first\nprobe discipline).  Composed with `mass_ratio_rigidity`, it excludes\n`m_w = C g^w φ(σ₀^w)^p` for *every* linear functional `φ`, not just for\n`net`: the observed lepton tower is log-concave (log-increments 5.332\nthen 2.822), while every member of this family is log-linear up to\n`O(q⁻²ⁿ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.linFunctionalK_binet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.linFunctionalK_binet","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/lepton_continuant_binet.lean#L171-L195","doc":"**Binet closed form for an arbitrary linear readout.**\n\n`(α b_n + β b_{n+1})(q + q⁻¹) = A qⁿ − (−1)ⁿ B q⁻ⁿ`, with\n\n```\n  A = α + β q        (the growing amplitude)\n  B = α − β q⁻¹      (the decaying amplitude)\n```\n\nThe whole two-parameter family therefore has the *same* two-term shape\nas `net`: one component growing like `qⁿ`, one decaying like `q⁻ⁿ`.\nChanging the readout only re-weights the two amplitudes; it cannot\nintroduce a third scale, because there is no third basis element. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.netK_eq_linFunctionalK","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.netK_eq_linFunctionalK","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/lepton_continuant_binet.lean#L166-L169","doc":"`net` is the linear functional with both coefficients `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.linFunctionalK","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.linFunctionalK","kind":"def","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/lepton_continuant_binet.lean#L158-L164","doc":"A linear functional on `H₂(q)` evaluated along the generation braids.\n\nWith `α = φ(1)` and `β = φ(σ₀)`, this is `φ(σ₀^(n+1))`, since\n`NF(σ₀^(n+1)) = b_n · 1 + b_{n+1} · σ₀`.  The index is the *lower*\ncontinuant index, so winding `w` corresponds to `n = w - 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.mass_ratio_rigidity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.mass_ratio_rigidity","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/lepton_continuant_binet.lean#L110-L131","doc":"**Ratio rigidity of the multiplicative bridge class.**\n\nIf a candidate mass map has the multiplicative shape\n`m n = C · gⁿ · (net n)^p` — which covers every power law, every\nexponential-times-power, and in particular the \"missing scale factor\"\n(`p = 1`, `g = 1`) that bean `qou-lsp9` posits — then each two-step\nmass ratio is `g²` times the corresponding net ratio raised to `p`.\n\nConsequence (the exclusion): the *only* thing that can make consecutive\nmass ratios differ is the variation of the net ratio.  By\n`morganVoyceBK_binet` that variation is the `O(q⁻²ⁿ)` remainder — 0.38%\nat the substrate `q₀` — so reproducing the observed 12.3× drop demands\n`p ≈ 667`, and `p` grows like `q²ⁿ` for any further generation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.netK","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.netK","kind":"def","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/lepton_continuant_binet.lean#L106-L108","doc":"The net normal-form coefficient `net(T(2,n)) = a_n + b_n = b_{n-1} + b_n`,\nfield-valued twin of `netCoeff`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.morganVoyceBK_binet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.morganVoyceBK_binet","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/lepton_continuant_binet.lean#L82-L104","doc":"**Binet closed form for the Morgan–Voyce continuant.**\n\n`b_n · (q + q⁻¹) = qⁿ − (−1)ⁿ (q⁻¹)ⁿ`, for any `q ≠ 0` in a field.\n\nThe two roots of `x² − (q − q⁻¹)x − 1` are `q` and `−q⁻¹`; this is the\nresulting Binet formula.  Its content is that the continuant is\ngeometric with ratio `q` up to an alternating remainder of size\n`q⁻ⁿ` — the fact that makes `net` log-linear in the winding number. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.morganVoyceBK_succ_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.morganVoyceBK_succ_succ","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/lepton_continuant_binet.lean#L78-L80","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.morganVoyceBK_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.morganVoyceBK_one","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/lepton_continuant_binet.lean#L76-L76","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.morganVoyceBK_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.morganVoyceBK_zero","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/lepton_continuant_binet.lean#L74-L74","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.morganVoyceBK","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.morganVoyceBK","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/lepton_continuant_binet.lean#L65-L72","doc":"The Morgan–Voyce continuant evaluated in a field at the Hecke\nparameter `h = q − q⁻¹`: `b 0 = 0`, `b 1 = 1`,\n`b (n+2) = h · b (n+1) + b n`.  This is the field-valued twin of\n`morganVoyceB : ℕ → Polynomial ℤ`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}